<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Carlson Trophic State Index from chlorophyll-a: 21 fixed preset table colors — <b>0-35 Oligotrophic</b> (chl 0.04-1.62) &rarr; <b>40-45 Mesotrophic</b> (chl 2.6-4.1) &rarr; <b>50-60 Eutrophic</b> (chl 6.4-20) &rarr; <b>65-100 Hypereutrophic</b> (chl 31-1,183). Every pixel shows its table row's exact color; the legend is the full table plus an isolated grey No-data swatch for cloud gaps. High TSI = biomass / activity, not toxins.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily); host fallback NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll Daily on the CoastWatch Central hub (noaacwN20VIIRSchlaDaily, same chlor_a OC3 variable)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Chlorophyll.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
